## Hints for Future Agents
The rule list in the for loop is maintained by hand and deliberately omits
rules/codex-mcp.md, since that rule tells Claude when to call Codex and means
nothing to Codex reading its own AGENTS.md. Adding a new file under rules/ does
NOT automatically reach Codex - you must add it to this loop. A glob would pick
up codex-mcp.md again, which is why this is not a glob.

The two skills are copied with cp -R, not symlinked, because Codex does not
read Claude Code plugin directories. That means they go stale when the plugin
version in the cache path changes. The rm -rf block at the top clears both
before copying so a reinstall is idempotent.

Source path is plugins/abatilo-core/skills/, i.e. the in-repo copy, not the
~/.claude/plugins/cache/ install.

